Indeed, this is due to the implementation of the function to convert to json 

Here is the old implementation :

`json(): string { return isPresent(this._body) ? JSON.stringify(this._body) : ''; }
`

Here is the new :

```
json(): any {
     if (isString(this._body)) {
       return Json.parse(<string>this._body);
     }

     if (this._body instanceof ArrayBuffer) {
       return Json.parse(this.text());
     }

     return this._body;
   }
```

Whereas the old one convert a json object to a string, the new one convert to a json object.

Therefore, if it is intended to pass json object as a string to the request, we have to update static_request.ts :

```
getBody(): any {
    switch (this.contentType) {
      case ContentType.JSON:
        return this.json();
      case ContentType.FORM:
        return this.text();
      case ContentType.FORM_DATA:
        return this._body;
      case ContentType.TEXT:
        return this.text();
      case ContentType.BLOB:
        return this.blob();
      case ContentType.ARRAY_BUFFER:
        return this.arrayBuffer();
      default:
        return null;
    }
  }
```

and change return for JSON to a text value.
